    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm runnign into a massive headache with our jenkins pipeline. the unit test stage is being super flaky. it'll pass fine one time, then fail the next with totally different error logs, even though we haven't touched the code. seems like it's something environmental or non-deterministic. any idea how i can start isolating what's causing these intermittent failures?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Flaky tests are incredibly frustrating, often stemming from external dependencies or timing issues. Start by running your tests locally in a clean environment to confirm the flakiness persists outside of Jenkins. Next, examine your Jenkins agent environment for resource contention, like CPU throttling or network latency, which can cause timeouts. Finally, look closely at test setup/teardown logic to see if shared state or race conditions are introduced.",
      "source": "target",
