    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i'll try adding some extra logging to the pre-test step. another thing is that the logs for the network connections seem totally random sometimes—like, it'll show a connection to a service that shouldn't even be in the test scope. it's like something is just popping up and then disappearing before i can catch it. any idea why we might be seeing these phantom connections?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Phantom network connections often point to background services or sidecar containers in the image that are not properly cleaned up or isolated. Investigate your container lifecycle to ensure all processes are truly stopped and the network namespace is reset after the test run. Sometimes, a poorly configured Docker volume or mounted network alias can persist connections across test executions. Review your Dockerfile or Kubernetes deployment specs for any lingering network setups.",
      "source": "target",
